  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of WASH and CP services for Rohingya refugees in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar and Bhasan Char</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to improve and sustain access to sufficient/safe water supply, functional sanitation facilities and prevent/respond to all forms of abuse/exploitation,/violence/neglect. This UNICEF project 1) provides safe water for drinking, cooking and/or personal hygiene for 48,543 people, 2) distributes WASH kits to 67,500 people and 3) provides access to protection activities and/or services through child-friendly spaces to 4,000 people. The project provides life-saving assistance to 48,543 people, including 12,621 women, 10,680 men, 25,242 children, and 485 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
